d. Between W9, T2, and T6, W9 is the most isolated (W9: 2 remaining, and no nearby tiles in my hand).\n\nReason: I want to preserve W3(\u00d73) as a valuable pung and W4(\u00d72) as a potential pair. W9 is the most isolated tile with no support from other tiles in my hand to form a chow. Discarding W9 keeps my hand closest to a valid winning structure while maintaining flexibility.\n\nAnswer: Play W9"}
